\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{The heat trace of a cycle}
\date{2026-11-06}

\p{Let #{C_N} be the cycle on #{N\ge 3} vertices. Use the
Laplacian displayed for the [spectral dimension](fdip-00CO),
with no factor #{N^2}. The function
#{j\mapsto \ue^{2\pi \ui kj/N}} is multiplied by
#{\ue^{2\pi \ui k/N}} under the shift that increases #{j}, and by
the conjugate phase under the inverse shift. Its eigenvalue
is
##{2-2\cos(2\pi k/N)=4\sin^2(\pi k/N).}
As #{k} runs through #{0,1,\ldots,N-1}, these #{N}
functions are orthogonal: the counting inner product of two
of them is a geometric sum, equal to #{N} when the
frequencies agree and equal to #{0} otherwise. They are
therefore a basis. The heat trace is
##{Z_N(t)=\sum_{k=0}^{N-1}
\ue^{-4t\sin^2(\pi k/N)}.}}
